1
00:00:01,758 --> 00:00:03,484
"Thanksgiving"

2
00:00:03,866 --> 00:00:06,253
<i>Thanksgiving around</i>
<i>here is all about tradition,</i>

3
00:00:06,448 --> 00:00:08,112
<i>spending time</i>
<i>with your family</i>

4
00:00:08,147 --> 00:00:10,159
<i>and being thankful</i>
<i>for everything you have.</i>

5
00:00:10,424 --> 00:00:12,271
<i>Of course, everyone has</i>
<i>their favorite thing.</i>

6
00:00:12,390 --> 00:00:14,489
<i>For Axl,</i>
<i>it's my cranberry sauce.</i>

7
00:00:15,575 --> 00:00:17,612
<i>For Mike,</i>
<i>it's my mashed potatoes.</i>

8
00:00:18,813 --> 00:00:21,638
<i>Sue and Brick love</i>
<i>my home-made pie.</i>

9
00:00:23,147 --> 00:00:24,172
<i>But what I love most</i>

10
00:00:24,207 --> 00:00:26,732
<i>is the warm, loving feeling</i>
<i>I get from...</i>

11
00:00:26,767 --> 00:00:28,722
<i>Saving up to 80%</i>

12
00:00:28,770 --> 00:00:30,386
<i>on the day</i>
<i>after Thanksgiving--</i>

13
00:00:30,421 --> 00:00:31,649
<i>Black Friday.</i>

14
00:00:33,268 --> 00:00:35,646
Okay, it's one week
to Thanksgiving.

15
00:00:35,647 --> 00:00:38,105
The mall opens at midnight,
so we've got to be prepared.

16
00:00:38,989 --> 00:00:41,941
Sue's on housewares,
Axl's on sporting goods,

17
00:00:41,976 --> 00:00:43,247
Brick can
ferret through the crowd,

18
00:00:43,282 --> 00:00:44,964
so he's on electronics.
Then we'll all rally

19
00:00:44,965 --> 00:00:47,646
- back at the escalator at 0100.
- Sir, yes, sir.

20
00:00:48,106 --> 00:00:50,308
Oh, and when you invite
your dad for Thanksgiving,

21
00:00:50,309 --> 00:00:52,253
can you ask him if he'll drop us off
and then wait for us

22
00:00:52,344 --> 00:00:54,676
so we don't get stuck behind some
slow driver looking for a spot?

23
00:00:57,280 --> 00:00:57,907
Mike...

24
00:00:58,499 --> 00:01:01,070
- Can't you invite him this year?
- He's <i>your</i> dad.

25
00:01:01,966 --> 00:01:02,995
He's such a pain!

26
00:01:03,030 --> 00:01:05,323
He'll say he doesn't want
to be a bother

27
00:01:05,324 --> 00:01:08,212
and drag it out until I end up
begging him, like always.

28
00:01:08,247 --> 00:01:11,349
Mike, someday that old pain in
the ass won't be here anymore,

29
00:01:11,384 --> 00:01:13,265
and then you'll be
begging to beg someone.

30
00:01:13,266 --> 00:01:15,276
Fine, I'll ask him,
but I'm not begging.

31
00:01:16,735 --> 00:01:18,638
Can we go
to the corn maze today?

32
00:01:19,238 --> 00:01:22,266
<i>Nothing says fall in</i>
<i>the Midwest like a corn maze.</i>

33
00:01:22,301 --> 00:01:24,442
<i>It's just about</i>
<i>the most fun thing ever.</i>

34
00:01:24,856 --> 00:01:28,413
Oh, I am <i>not</i> dragging my butt
through another corn maze.

35
00:01:28,414 --> 00:01:30,848
- I just can't do it.
- But I've never been.

36
00:01:31,160 --> 00:01:33,595
What are you talking about?
We've been a million times.

37
00:01:33,630 --> 00:01:36,450
With Sue and Axl.
I never got to go.

38
00:01:37,216 --> 00:01:38,586
I never get
to go anywhere.

39
00:01:38,724 --> 00:01:40,596
That's 'cause
you're their least favorite.

40
00:01:40,931 --> 00:01:44,032
<i>Ironically, at the moment,</i>
<i>Axl was my least favorite.</i>

41
00:01:44,750 --> 00:01:46,056
Okay, we'll find a time
to take you,

42
00:01:46,091 --> 00:01:47,277
but today isn't it.

43
00:01:48,441 --> 00:01:51,238
Hey, can I go snowmobiling
with my friends on Thanksgiving?

44
00:01:51,273 --> 00:01:51,906
No.

45
00:01:53,508 --> 00:01:56,008
No, dude, I can't. She just
totally freaked out on me!

46
00:01:56,559 --> 00:01:59,337
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!
Oh, my God! Oh, my God!

47
00:02:00,550 --> 00:02:01,798
We were square dancing
in gym class,

48
00:02:01,833 --> 00:02:02,653
and this boy Brad Bottig

49
00:02:02,688 --> 00:02:04,443
kept asking me to dance
all week, and then today

50
00:02:04,478 --> 00:02:06,717
on the third allemande left,
he asked me to be his girlfriend!

51
00:02:07,940 --> 00:02:10,128
Oh, my God!
I have a boyfriend!

52
00:02:13,940 --> 00:02:14,940
She's just a kid, Frankie.

53
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:16,088
I don't know if I like this.

54
00:02:16,123 --> 00:02:19,179
Oh, this is just
an innocent junior high thing.

55
00:02:19,214 --> 00:02:22,018
- Don't you think we can trust her?
- It's the guy I don't trust.

56
00:02:22,340 --> 00:02:24,138
I took square dancing
for one reason--

57
00:02:24,173 --> 00:02:25,371
It's a meat market.

58
00:02:27,534 --> 00:02:30,605
60% off on
a power sander for Mike,

59
00:02:30,640 --> 00:02:34,139
100 barrettes for Sue
at Claire's for $1,

60
00:02:34,174 --> 00:02:36,551
2-for-1 cargo pants
for Brick.

61
00:02:37,273 --> 00:02:38,836
Look at me!
I'm trembling.

62
00:02:39,295 --> 00:02:40,737
I think what I'm most
looking forward to

63
00:02:40,772 --> 00:02:42,995
is watching home movies,
singing around the piano.

64
00:02:43,030 --> 00:02:45,204
My niece, who I haven't seen
in 14 years is coming in.

65
00:02:45,797 --> 00:02:48,378
I gotta get air mattresses
just to host everyone!

66
00:02:48,769 --> 00:02:51,728
<i>Bob, Hometown Buffet</i>
<i>called about</i>

67
00:02:51,763 --> 00:02:54,642
<i>your Thanksgiving reservation.</i>
<i>They want to know if</i>

68
00:02:54,677 --> 00:02:57,151
<i>you'd share a two-top</i>
<i>with a widower.</i>

69
00:02:57,761 --> 00:03:00,111
- We eat at 6:00.
- Oh, thank you!

70
00:03:00,712 --> 00:03:03,622
All right, team, bring it in.
Take a knee.

71
00:03:04,495 --> 00:03:06,873
Sales are
at an all-time low.

72
00:03:07,413 --> 00:03:11,017
That is why I'm switching
to a 365-day schedule,

73
00:03:11,052 --> 00:03:13,153
like that diner out
on Route 7.

74
00:03:13,891 --> 00:03:14,898
They do very well.

75
00:03:15,250 --> 00:03:15,910
Wait, wait, wait.

76
00:03:16,430 --> 00:03:19,510
Are you saying that
we're working on Thanksgiving?

77
00:03:21,183 --> 00:03:24,266
Mr. Ehlert,
that is just wrong.

78
00:03:24,935 --> 00:03:27,725
Well, so is taking the country
away from a bunch of Indians,

79
00:03:28,195 --> 00:03:29,780
but aren't you glad
we did?

80
00:03:37,397 --> 00:03:38,532
Mr. Ehlert?

81
00:03:38,774 --> 00:03:40,345
What now?
Tampon machine empty?

82
00:03:41,708 --> 00:03:44,207
N-no, actually, sir,
I was wondering

83
00:03:44,242 --> 00:03:46,827
if I could possibly,
in any way,

84
00:03:47,083 --> 00:03:50,153
have Thanksgiving off
to spend with my family?

85
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,894
Okay, we're gonna
play a little game called

86
00:03:51,929 --> 00:03:53,609
"I be you, you be me."

87
00:03:54,071 --> 00:03:55,259
"Mr. Ehlert,

88
00:03:55,294 --> 00:03:58,483
"I know I'm the newest employee
with the worst sales record,

89
00:03:58,669 --> 00:04:01,463
"and even though I whine
about equality for women

90
00:04:01,498 --> 00:04:04,012
"in the workplace,
can I have Thanksgiving off

91
00:04:04,047 --> 00:04:05,980
"so I can hug my family
all day long,

92
00:04:06,015 --> 00:04:08,377
"even though two minutes ago,
you said I had to work?"

93
00:04:09,112 --> 00:04:09,941
Yes?

94
00:04:10,966 --> 00:04:13,156
Okay, I'm me again.
No!

95
00:04:13,368 --> 00:04:14,892
Please.

96
00:04:14,927 --> 00:04:17,914
My family needs Thanksgiving,
and I'm the mom.

97
00:04:18,224 --> 00:04:20,728
I have to cook in the morning,
and we eat in the afternoon.

98
00:04:21,100 --> 00:04:23,140
Fine. You can
work the evening shift.

99
00:04:24,079 --> 00:04:26,554
And if you're still here,
you can work all day Christmas.

100
00:04:27,553 --> 00:04:29,940
Christmas?
Thanksgiving?

101
00:04:29,975 --> 00:04:30,873
This man's crazy.

102
00:04:30,908 --> 00:04:33,129
Who the hell buys a car
on Thanksgiving, anyway?

103
00:04:33,164 --> 00:04:36,342
I know it sucks, but I'm not
gonna let it ruin our day.

104
00:04:36,512 --> 00:04:38,661
We'll eat earlier,
then I'll go in to work,

105
00:04:38,696 --> 00:04:40,417
then I'll meet you and the kids
at the mall at midnight.

106
00:04:40,452 --> 00:04:42,632
And be sure to tell your dad
about the time change.

107
00:04:44,795 --> 00:04:47,963
- You haven't invited him yet.
- I will, woman. Back off.

108
00:04:50,618 --> 00:04:51,874
Mom, Dad?

109
00:04:52,316 --> 00:04:55,577
This is brad...
my boyfriend.

110
00:04:59,725 --> 00:05:01,161
- Be cool.
- Yeah.

111
00:05:01,729 --> 00:05:03,157
Hi, Brad!

112
00:05:03,278 --> 00:05:04,349
Hi, you guys.

113
00:05:04,420 --> 00:05:07,668
Oh my gosh, I'm super excited
to finally meet my GF's P's.

114
00:05:07,859 --> 00:05:10,670
<i>"Girlfriend's parents."</i>
<i>I looked it up later.</i>

115
00:05:10,905 --> 00:05:14,065
Well, we are so excited
to meet you, too, Brad,

116
00:05:14,100 --> 00:05:15,520
- aren't we, Mike?
- Yep.

117
00:05:15,897 --> 00:05:19,525
So you--you, uh, like to...
square-dance, huh?

118
00:05:19,560 --> 00:05:21,250
Oh, I just love
square dancing.

119
00:05:21,285 --> 00:05:22,765
Well, all types of dance,
really, you know?

120
00:05:23,060 --> 00:05:24,862
Ballet, tap, rhythmic.

121
00:05:25,452 --> 00:05:28,022
O.M.G., is that
vintage flannel?

122
00:05:28,312 --> 00:05:30,270
No. Just--just old.

123
00:05:30,305 --> 00:05:32,005
And super cute.

124
00:05:32,898 --> 00:05:33,844
Well, thanks.

125
00:05:34,309 --> 00:05:36,306
We're gonna go get
my "Flashdance" CD,

126
00:05:36,341 --> 00:05:38,931
and Brad's gonna show me
some choreography he made up.

127
00:05:44,953 --> 00:05:47,416
Well, he seems nice.

128
00:05:47,451 --> 00:05:48,079
Very!

129
00:05:48,581 --> 00:05:50,046
- Still worried?
- No.

130
00:05:50,366 --> 00:05:52,165
You think we should
say something to Sue?

131
00:05:52,260 --> 00:05:54,844
No. She'll figure it out
eventually, or he will.

132
00:05:58,341 --> 00:06:00,162
What?

133
00:06:01,336 --> 00:06:04,022
The Black Friday sale
is earlier this year.

134
00:06:04,057 --> 00:06:07,660
- What's earlier than midnight?
- 6:00 on Thanksgiving Day.

135
00:06:07,695 --> 00:06:10,172
We have <i>got</i> to be there
when the doors open!

136
00:06:10,574 --> 00:06:12,990
Look, the first
100 customers get 20% off

137
00:06:13,025 --> 00:06:15,878
and a free soft pretzel.
All right. Okay.

138
00:06:15,913 --> 00:06:19,356
I'm just gonna have to
go in and...

139
00:06:19,750 --> 00:06:21,915
I'll ask Mr. Ehlert
for a different shift.

140
00:06:23,501 --> 00:06:25,421
I know
it's against the rules, but...

141
00:06:25,745 --> 00:06:27,791
can Brad and I
hang out in my room?

142
00:06:27,958 --> 00:06:30,042
Sure. Close the door
if we're bothering you.

143
00:06:30,728 --> 00:06:34,324
<i>So Mike finally went</i>
<i>to ask his dad to Thanksgiving,</i>

144
00:06:34,767 --> 00:06:36,843
<i>which sounds easier</i>
<i>than it is,</i>

145
00:06:37,225 --> 00:06:39,677
<i>'cause Big Mike's</i>
<i>kind of a hoarder</i>

146
00:06:39,712 --> 00:06:41,425
<i>who doesn't like to</i>
<i>leave his house.</i>

147
00:06:41,835 --> 00:06:44,774
<i>Maybe 'cause he's got too much</i>
<i>pride to accept an invitation,</i>

148
00:06:45,297 --> 00:06:48,091
<i>Or maybe 'cause there's too</i>
<i>much crap blocking the door.</i>

149
00:06:48,463 --> 00:06:50,075
I know
you're home, Dad.

150
00:06:50,110 --> 00:06:52,353
Montgomery Ward went
out of business ten years ago.

151
00:06:54,659 --> 00:06:55,635
It's good to know.

152
00:07:01,600 --> 00:07:03,557
So Thanksgiving's coming up.

153
00:07:04,149 --> 00:07:05,587
Is it, now?

154
00:07:06,018 --> 00:07:08,400
Oh, well,
the calendar says it's today.

155
00:07:08,753 --> 00:07:11,121
Yeah, the calendar's
four years old, Dad.

156
00:07:12,772 --> 00:07:13,208
Oh.

157
00:07:13,963 --> 00:07:16,785
Anyway, Frankie's putting
together a nice dinner.

158
00:07:17,490 --> 00:07:18,094
You should come.

159
00:07:18,129 --> 00:07:20,272
I don't want
to be a bother.

160
00:07:20,597 --> 00:07:21,750
You're not a bother, Dad.

161
00:07:22,232 --> 00:07:25,169
Well, don't go
making turkey on my account.

162
00:07:25,204 --> 00:07:26,434
We're making it anyway.

163
00:07:27,476 --> 00:07:28,560
All of America is.

164
00:07:30,148 --> 00:07:32,150
If I come,
you'll just have to

165
00:07:32,185 --> 00:07:34,066
get another chair
out of the garage--

166
00:07:34,627 --> 00:07:36,087
All that hassle...

167
00:07:37,040 --> 00:07:38,748
Okay, Dad,
we're eating at 4:00.

168
00:07:38,783 --> 00:07:40,698
Come if you want.
Don't if you don't.

169
00:07:41,124 --> 00:07:43,124
That's not
much of an invite, is it?

170
00:07:47,431 --> 00:07:50,187
<i>Fortunately, not everyone's</i>
<i>too proud to beg.</i>

171
00:07:50,667 --> 00:07:53,833
Sir, I just found out
my Aunt Ginny

172
00:07:53,868 --> 00:07:56,733
needs emergency surgery
on the night of Thanksgiving,

173
00:07:56,768 --> 00:07:58,641
so could I please switch
to the afternoon shift

174
00:07:58,642 --> 00:08:00,253
so I can take her
to the hospital?

175
00:08:00,288 --> 00:08:01,405
Of course.

176
00:08:01,836 --> 00:08:04,188
- Thank you, Mr. Ehlert.
- And you're working Easter.

177
00:08:07,169 --> 00:08:08,111
Okay.

178
00:08:09,850 --> 00:08:11,331
Got the new
Thanksgiving schedule.

179
00:08:12,733 --> 00:08:13,821
It's a little funky.

180
00:08:13,856 --> 00:08:16,105
We're gonna have to eat dessert
in the car on the way home,

181
00:08:16,140 --> 00:08:18,413
and there's one little patch
midday where I'm gonna have to

182
00:08:18,448 --> 00:08:21,939
be in two places at the same time,
but I think a test drive

183
00:08:21,974 --> 00:08:23,682
or a long bathroom break
will take care of it.

184
00:08:23,717 --> 00:08:26,339
So, yeah, I think
I pretty much nailed it.

185
00:08:26,932 --> 00:08:28,734
I don't see
the corn maze on here.

186
00:08:28,769 --> 00:08:31,775
It's only open in the morning,
then they're plowing it down.

187
00:08:32,317 --> 00:08:35,067
Brick, I'm gonna teach you

188
00:08:35,102 --> 00:08:37,424
a little phrase that I think
will come in very handy.

189
00:08:37,824 --> 00:08:39,437
I call it, "Oh, well."

190
00:08:41,041 --> 00:08:42,942
You know, we went to Disneyland
once before you were born.

191
00:08:42,977 --> 00:08:44,093
It was awesome.

192
00:08:44,916 --> 00:08:48,028
<i>Poor Brick. He was</i>
<i>the forgotten third child,</i>

193
00:08:48,063 --> 00:08:50,589
<i>but there was no way I could</i>
<i>go back in to Mr. Ehlert,</i>

194
00:08:50,624 --> 00:08:52,581
<i>and he was just gonna have</i>
<i>to understand that.</i>

195
00:08:53,546 --> 00:08:55,762
So now the kidney's coming in
on an earlier flight,

196
00:08:55,763 --> 00:08:57,324
which means I need to
switch to the morning shift

197
00:08:57,394 --> 00:09:00,692
so I can drive the kidney to
the hospital. It's an H.M.O.

198
00:09:02,416 --> 00:09:02,955
Okay.

199
00:09:03,337 --> 00:09:04,525
I did it.

200
00:09:05,506 --> 00:09:07,957
It was hard,
but I figured it out.

201
00:09:08,961 --> 00:09:11,635
I put the turkey in tonight.
We all set our alarms.

202
00:09:11,670 --> 00:09:14,545
We eat dinner at dawn.
I'll work until 11:00,

203
00:09:14,580 --> 00:09:16,207
then we record
the football game

204
00:09:16,242 --> 00:09:17,952
while we take Brick
to the corn maze,

205
00:09:17,987 --> 00:09:21,235
come home, clean up, get to
the mall, and for dessert,

206
00:09:21,631 --> 00:09:23,589
we split a dairy-free yogurt
at the food court.

207
00:09:24,611 --> 00:09:25,659
I have a coupon.

208
00:09:26,372 --> 00:09:28,358
That sounds like
the worst Thanksgiving ever.

209
00:09:28,393 --> 00:09:31,371
It really does.
Can I go to Brad's instead?

210
00:09:31,406 --> 00:09:34,040
I <i>really</i> should be with
my boyfriend on Thanksgiving.

211
00:09:34,424 --> 00:09:36,315
I really just care
about the corn maze.

212
00:09:36,938 --> 00:09:40,590
No. Thanksgiving is
about family.

213
00:09:40,625 --> 00:09:44,079
We have Aunt Edie and Aunt Ginny
coming over and Big Mike.

214
00:09:44,114 --> 00:09:45,333
Uh, maybe.

215
00:09:45,903 --> 00:09:46,373
Maybe?

216
00:09:46,408 --> 00:09:47,466
Probably not.

217
00:09:48,318 --> 00:09:50,825
I've asked you
to do one thing--

218
00:09:50,860 --> 00:09:52,090
Get your dad to come!

219
00:09:52,125 --> 00:09:55,782
Do you people realize what
I have gone through this week

220
00:09:55,817 --> 00:09:57,026
to make Thanksgiving
happen?

221
00:09:57,061 --> 00:09:58,518
And now you guys
don't appreciate--

222
00:09:58,553 --> 00:10:00,882
Oh, hey,
that's my ride.

223
00:10:01,193 --> 00:10:02,871
Hey.

224
00:10:03,611 --> 00:10:06,359
I figured once my friends came
to pick me up for snowmobiling,

225
00:10:06,394 --> 00:10:08,341
you'd be too embarrassed
to say no.

226
00:10:08,376 --> 00:10:09,796
You figured wrong.

227
00:10:13,207 --> 00:10:16,274
<i>No!</i>

228
00:10:19,278 --> 00:10:19,963
You know what?

229
00:10:20,755 --> 00:10:22,672
You don't care,
I don't care.

230
00:10:23,009 --> 00:10:23,752
Thanksgiving...

231
00:10:24,243 --> 00:10:25,740
Canceled.

232
00:10:30,316 --> 00:10:31,621
Way to go, Brick.

233
00:10:39,961 --> 00:10:41,316
Where's the good smell?

234
00:10:42,263 --> 00:10:44,568
Wait. Did Mom really
cancel Thanksgiving?

235
00:10:44,801 --> 00:10:47,543
- Yeah. She's at work.
- Well, who's gonna make the turkey?

236
00:10:47,544 --> 00:10:49,271
Who's gonna bake
the frozen pies?

237
00:10:49,272 --> 00:10:51,049
Who's gonna open
the can of cranberry sauce?

238
00:10:51,365 --> 00:10:51,990
Not Mom.

239
00:10:52,165 --> 00:10:55,515
Dude. That sucks.

240
00:10:55,785 --> 00:10:57,842
That's why we're gonna
pick up the slack

241
00:10:57,954 --> 00:11:00,946
and pull Thanksgiving
together <i>for</i> her.

242
00:11:00,957 --> 00:11:02,250
That sounds hard.

243
00:11:02,814 --> 00:11:05,016
It's not hard.
It's not hard at all.

244
00:11:06,055 --> 00:11:06,535
Watch.

245
00:11:15,359 --> 00:11:17,333
<i>So what if we had</i>
<i>no Thanksgiving?</i>

246
00:11:17,616 --> 00:11:19,945
<i>Just another day,</i>
<i>just another dinner.</i>

247
00:11:20,053 --> 00:11:22,405
<i>Not like anyone</i>
<i>cared anyway.</i>

248
00:11:22,440 --> 00:11:25,115
Guess who made yams
with little marshmallows

249
00:11:25,150 --> 00:11:26,410
for Thanksgiving dinner?

250
00:11:26,760 --> 00:11:29,679
Oh, my God. I forgot
to tell you. I canceled that.

251
00:11:30,442 --> 00:11:32,260
A phone call
would have been nice.

252
00:11:35,606 --> 00:11:39,515
Seven hours? I'm gonna have
to barbecue this thing.

253
00:11:39,550 --> 00:11:40,178
While I do that,

254
00:11:40,213 --> 00:11:41,924
I want you to take your brother
to the corn maze.

255
00:11:41,959 --> 00:11:43,712
Oh, God. Do you just,
like, stay up late

256
00:11:43,747 --> 00:11:45,117
trying to figure out ways
to ruin my life?

257
00:11:45,152 --> 00:11:45,925
Yes.

258
00:11:47,778 --> 00:11:49,326
Oh, hey, can I invite Brad
over to help?

259
00:11:49,722 --> 00:11:51,260
It's Thanksgiving.
Won't his parents miss him?

260
00:11:51,702 --> 00:11:54,176
Oh, they're just so excited
he has a girlfriend.

261
00:11:55,359 --> 00:11:56,089
I could see that.

262
00:11:56,786 --> 00:11:58,482
I wonder what our kids
will look like.

263
00:11:58,517 --> 00:12:00,899
Mm. Depends what country
you get 'em from, right?

264
00:12:01,647 --> 00:12:02,225
Axl.

265
00:12:06,406 --> 00:12:08,173
Wow.
Now I get why they say

266
00:12:08,208 --> 00:12:10,129
the corn's as high
as an elephant's eye.

267
00:12:10,659 --> 00:12:11,900
<i>Elephant.</i>

268
00:12:11,935 --> 00:12:13,121
You know when I saw
an elephant?

269
00:12:13,472 --> 00:12:15,368
When Mom and Dad took us
to Africa on that safari.

270
00:12:15,769 --> 00:12:17,041
They did not.

271
00:12:17,248 --> 00:12:18,494
Did, too.
I peed in the Nile.

272
00:12:22,168 --> 00:12:22,974
'Sup?

273
00:12:29,214 --> 00:12:29,728
Brick?

274
00:12:30,797 --> 00:12:32,131
<i>Brick?</i>

275
00:12:35,002 --> 00:12:35,484
Brick!

276
00:12:37,222 --> 00:12:39,844
<i>There we were,</i>
<i>stuck working on Thanksgiving,</i>

277
00:12:39,845 --> 00:12:42,103
<i>waiting for customers</i>
<i>who'd never come.</i>

278
00:12:42,138 --> 00:12:43,961
This is insane!

279
00:12:43,962 --> 00:12:47,301
Nobody's gonna buy a car today.
Why are we even here?

280
00:12:48,027 --> 00:12:51,359
Oh, my--I just want to go home,
eat with my family,

281
00:12:51,394 --> 00:12:54,549
enjoy some holiday savings
and a free hot pretzel.

282
00:12:54,891 --> 00:12:57,061
That is my right
as an American.

283
00:12:57,096 --> 00:12:58,575
He can't take that away.

284
00:12:58,682 --> 00:13:01,565
Frankie is right. We should say
something to <r. Ehlert.

285
00:13:02,423 --> 00:13:05,040
He can't say no to all of us.
Right?

286
00:13:05,075 --> 00:13:06,289
- That's right.
- Let's do this.

287
00:13:06,369 --> 00:13:06,899
Let's do it.

288
00:13:14,877 --> 00:13:15,564
Mr. Ehlert?

289
00:13:18,443 --> 00:13:19,657
We have something
to say.

290
00:13:20,977 --> 00:13:21,444
"We"?

291
00:13:24,604 --> 00:13:27,928
I guess it's I.
<i>I</i> have something to say.

292
00:13:29,033 --> 00:13:31,169
It's Thanksgiving,
Mr. Ehlert.

293
00:13:31,646 --> 00:13:34,868
We're supposed to be
with family, people we love,

294
00:13:34,903 --> 00:13:37,832
not people we sort of like
because we work with them.

295
00:13:41,334 --> 00:13:42,803
My wife left me.

296
00:13:45,490 --> 00:13:46,157
Oh.

297
00:13:48,014 --> 00:13:48,783
Brick?

298
00:13:50,398 --> 00:13:51,213
Brick.

299
00:13:55,409 --> 00:13:57,797
Hey, have you seen
a little kid about...

300
00:13:59,282 --> 00:13:59,882
This tall?

301
00:13:59,917 --> 00:14:02,403
I lost my little brother,
you know.

302
00:14:02,438 --> 00:14:06,103
I lost my little brother
in the corn maze in '53.

303
00:14:06,897 --> 00:14:08,566
When the wind
rustles the leaves,

304
00:14:09,128 --> 00:14:10,698
I can still
hear him calling.

305
00:14:12,616 --> 00:14:13,431
Brick!

306
00:14:14,901 --> 00:14:16,606
<i>Now it all made sense.</i>

307
00:14:16,641 --> 00:14:19,214
<i>Mr. Ehlert wanted to stay open</i>
<i>on Thanksgiving</i>

308
00:14:19,249 --> 00:14:21,301
<i>'cause he didn't want to face</i>
<i>the holidays alone.</i>

309
00:14:22,073 --> 00:14:23,317
Sit with me, Frances.

310
00:14:23,675 --> 00:14:26,157
Well, I-I did have
a kidney to pick up,

311
00:14:26,650 --> 00:14:27,713
but, uh...

312
00:14:28,868 --> 00:14:29,748
Okay.

313
00:14:37,512 --> 00:14:37,971
Brick!

314
00:14:39,516 --> 00:14:41,596
Brick! Brick!

315
00:14:42,058 --> 00:14:43,122
Where are you?

316
00:14:43,123 --> 00:14:45,270
Better find him
before they start plowin'.

317
00:14:45,781 --> 00:14:48,679
Can't see a little boy from
high up on the corn chopper.

318
00:14:49,907 --> 00:14:50,818
Brick!

319
00:14:51,621 --> 00:14:54,046
Brick! Brick!

320
00:15:01,928 --> 00:15:03,514
Aunt Ginny and Aunt Edie
are here.

321
00:15:04,085 --> 00:15:06,247
Great.
Maybe they can help.

322
00:15:06,442 --> 00:15:07,849
<i>Aunt Ginny and Aunt Edie</i>

323
00:15:07,884 --> 00:15:10,106
<i>haven't been able to help</i>
<i>since 1978.</i>

324
00:15:15,104 --> 00:15:16,431
Happy Thanksgiving!

325
00:15:19,563 --> 00:15:21,072
It's my boyfriend!

326
00:15:21,535 --> 00:15:24,188
I made you this centerpiece
from the bounties of nature.

327
00:15:24,671 --> 00:15:27,246
Oh, God.
You're so romantic.

328
00:15:28,254 --> 00:15:29,268
P.S., Mr. Heck,

329
00:15:29,303 --> 00:15:31,908
there's a strange man
parked in front of your house.

330
00:15:43,035 --> 00:15:44,229
Hey, Dad.
What are you doing?

331
00:15:49,213 --> 00:15:51,233
Just listening
to the game.

332
00:15:52,276 --> 00:15:53,580
You drove across town
for that?

333
00:15:54,163 --> 00:15:56,033
Reception's
better over here.

334
00:15:56,829 --> 00:16:01,054
Plus I heard someone
threw a bread maker out

335
00:16:01,089 --> 00:16:01,986
in this neighborhood.

336
00:16:02,951 --> 00:16:05,620
Well, as long as you're here,
you might as well come in.

337
00:16:06,213 --> 00:16:07,470
We're barbecuing
a whole turkey.

338
00:16:07,505 --> 00:16:09,084
I don't want to be a bother.

339
00:16:09,119 --> 00:16:11,984
You're not a bother, Dad.
I want you to come in.

340
00:16:16,691 --> 00:16:18,003
Please.
I'm begging you.

341
00:16:19,257 --> 00:16:20,759
Thanksgiving wouldn't be
the same without you.

342
00:16:20,794 --> 00:16:22,803
We wouldn't know what to do
if you didn't come.

343
00:16:22,929 --> 00:16:25,021
<i>Yep,</i>
<i>no stopping tradition.</i>

344
00:16:28,797 --> 00:16:30,717
Guess I can listen
to this inside.

345
00:16:35,276 --> 00:16:36,018
Brick!

346
00:16:36,769 --> 00:16:37,875
Brick! Hey!

347
00:16:37,910 --> 00:16:39,275
Oh, my God!
Please help me find my brother!

348
00:16:39,333 --> 00:16:42,160
- He's lost, and I'm so scared!
- Um, what's he wearing?

349
00:16:42,195 --> 00:16:44,767
Uh, he's got, like,
a green jacket and a yellow hat,

350
00:16:44,802 --> 00:16:47,897
and oh, my God,
he's dressed like corn.

351
00:16:48,121 --> 00:16:49,689
We are never gonna
find him in here!

352
00:16:50,150 --> 00:16:50,728
Hi.

353
00:16:51,157 --> 00:16:53,226
Brick! Oh, my God.

354
00:16:54,020 --> 00:16:55,205
I'm never letting you
out of my sight, okay?

355
00:16:55,240 --> 00:16:57,913
Never, ever, ever, never,
ever again, all right?

356
00:16:59,587 --> 00:17:00,247
'Sup?

357
00:17:06,862 --> 00:17:09,944
You know what, Frances?
Go home.

358
00:17:10,902 --> 00:17:13,001
Go be with
your perfect family.

359
00:17:13,472 --> 00:17:14,350
Perfect?

360
00:17:16,055 --> 00:17:19,118
My son
wanted to leave me

361
00:17:19,153 --> 00:17:22,120
and spend Thanksgiving
with his friends.

362
00:17:22,155 --> 00:17:23,021
- No!
- Yeah.

363
00:17:23,089 --> 00:17:27,618
And don't even get me started
on my husband and his dad. Ohh.

364
00:17:32,589 --> 00:17:33,805
Grandpa Big Mike!

365
00:17:34,239 --> 00:17:36,136
- Boys!
- How was the corn maze?

366
00:17:36,171 --> 00:17:39,213
- Axl hugged me.
- Oh, shut up, dweeb.

367
00:17:39,870 --> 00:17:41,209
I love you.
I love you so much.

368
00:17:42,040 --> 00:17:43,385
You know what,
Mr. Ehlert?

369
00:17:43,495 --> 00:17:45,297
I can c-call you that,
right, mr. Ehlert?

370
00:17:45,332 --> 00:17:46,010
Mm.

371
00:17:46,512 --> 00:17:48,298
I used
to be scared of you.

372
00:17:49,222 --> 00:17:49,948
I was.

373
00:17:50,016 --> 00:17:52,264
But you're just a big,
old teddy bear, right?

374
00:17:52,919 --> 00:17:55,333
Marcy used to call me
her teddy bear.

375
00:17:56,821 --> 00:17:59,593
Damn shame she couldn't get
over me working Thanksgiving.

376
00:18:01,049 --> 00:18:01,828
Wait.

377
00:18:03,405 --> 00:18:04,104
Hold on.

378
00:18:05,362 --> 00:18:06,270
Are you kidding me?

379
00:18:07,535 --> 00:18:11,058
I thought you were working today
because your wife left you,

380
00:18:11,093 --> 00:18:15,432
but your wife left you
because you're working today?

381
00:18:15,467 --> 00:18:17,891
Kept saying, "You can't
keep the dealership open!

382
00:18:18,452 --> 00:18:21,071
Your only daughter's
coming in from Hawaii."

383
00:18:22,636 --> 00:18:25,165
She can't tell <i>me</i>
what to do.

384
00:18:26,312 --> 00:18:28,568
Oh, my God!

385
00:18:29,420 --> 00:18:33,806
How dare you make me
waste my Thanksgiving

386
00:18:33,841 --> 00:18:35,573
feeling sorry for you?

387
00:18:35,864 --> 00:18:37,443
You don't deserve
my sorry.

388
00:18:37,709 --> 00:18:40,226
You know who deserves
my sorry? Me.

389
00:18:41,008 --> 00:18:41,985
I'm going home.

390
00:18:43,058 --> 00:18:45,899
And fire me,
don't fire me,

391
00:18:45,934 --> 00:18:46,873
I don't care.

392
00:18:49,107 --> 00:18:51,507
But if you're on the fence,
don't fire me.

393
00:18:59,082 --> 00:19:00,445
Thanks for the ride, Bob!

394
00:19:00,976 --> 00:19:02,512
She's here.
Let's surprise her.

395
00:19:19,165 --> 00:19:20,349
Surprise!

396
00:19:20,384 --> 00:19:22,292
Ohh!

397
00:19:23,055 --> 00:19:24,256
Happy Thanksgiving, honey.

398
00:19:25,480 --> 00:19:28,795
<i>They</i> did <i>care.</i>
<i>They</i> are <i>perfect.</i>

399
00:19:29,712 --> 00:19:30,413
Come sit down.

400
00:19:30,448 --> 00:19:31,815
Sit down, sit down.

401
00:19:33,078 --> 00:19:35,965
Oh, and this all looks
so yummy.

402
00:19:36,874 --> 00:19:38,412
- Hey. Mm.
- Mm.

403
00:19:39,263 --> 00:19:40,496
Frankie, you forgot your...

404
00:19:41,669 --> 00:19:42,833
"Canceled dinner"?

405
00:19:43,946 --> 00:19:45,842
God, this is like high school
all over again.

406
00:19:45,877 --> 00:19:48,891
Oh, no, Bob.
They surprised me...

407
00:19:48,926 --> 00:19:52,458
My wonderful, sweet family.

408
00:19:55,415 --> 00:19:58,733
I am so sorry
I yelled at you.

409
00:19:58,768 --> 00:20:01,327
- We're sorry, too, honey.
- We love you, Mom.

410
00:20:01,724 --> 00:20:02,814
I love you, too.

411
00:20:04,315 --> 00:20:05,830
I got extra yams in the car...

412
00:20:06,562 --> 00:20:08,026
with little marshmallows.

413
00:20:11,706 --> 00:20:12,858
Here comes the gravy.

414
00:20:19,204 --> 00:20:21,899
I'm--I'm gonna go cry
in the toilet.

415
00:20:21,934 --> 00:20:23,008
Mike, come hold my hair.

416
00:20:23,043 --> 00:20:25,125
<i>And that's the last thing</i>
<i>I remembered.</i>

417
00:20:26,213 --> 00:20:27,619
<i>And though I didn't</i>
<i>make it to the mall,</i>

418
00:20:27,654 --> 00:20:30,148
- <i>I was there in spirit.</i>
- Frankie?

419
00:20:33,993 --> 00:20:35,521
Oh, what did I buy?

420
00:20:36,376 --> 00:20:38,629
Power sander, 80% off.

421
00:20:40,323 --> 00:20:42,501
Did we make
the houseware sale on time?

422
00:20:43,073 --> 00:20:44,516
We got the bacon press.

423
00:20:45,248 --> 00:20:46,750
Good girl.

424
00:20:47,691 --> 00:20:48,776
<i>Thanksgiving's the time</i>

425
00:20:48,811 --> 00:20:50,702
<i>you appreciate</i>
<i>your family the most.</i>

426
00:20:50,737 --> 00:20:53,617
<i>But the one Thanksgiving</i>
<i>I didn't spend with my family,</i>

427
00:20:54,073 --> 00:20:56,160
<i>I appreciated them</i>
<i>more than ever.</i>

428
00:20:56,577 --> 00:21:00,632
See, kids? Let this be a lesson.
Drinking is not cool.

429
00:21:01,090 --> 00:21:03,207
Mike, I told them
I had the flu.

430
00:21:04,461 --> 00:21:07,457
See, kids,
lying is also not cool.

431
00:21:09,554 --> 00:21:13,702
Honey, why don't we close
this up just a little bit?

432
00:21:14,090 --> 00:21:15,338
There you go.
We have company.

433
00:21:16,009 --> 00:21:17,883
Okay. Night, honey.
Happy Thanksgiving.

434
00:21:20,466 --> 00:21:23,576
Sync and Edits: VeRdiKT
[Subscene.com / Addic7ed.com]
